     lliibbbbee interfaces with libzfs to provide a set of functions for various
     operations regarding ZFS boot environments including "deep" boot environ‐
     ments in which a boot environments has child datasets.

     A context structure is passed to each function, allowing for a small
     amount of state to be retained, such as errors from previous operations.
     lliibbbbee may be configured to print the corresponding error message to
     stderr when an error is encountered with lliibbbbee__pprriinntt__oonn__eerrrroorr().

     All functions returning an _i_n_t return 0 on success, or a lliibbbbee errno oth‐
     erwise as described in _D_I_A_G_N_O_S_T_I_C_S.

     The lliibbbbee__iinniitt() function takes an optional BE root and initializes
     lliibbbbee, returning a _l_i_b_b_e___h_a_n_d_l_e___t _* on success, or NULL on error.  If a
     BE root is supplied, lliibbbbee will only operate out of that pool and BE
     root.  An error may occur if:

     ••   _/_b_o_o_t and _/ are not on the same filesystem and device,

     ••   libzfs fails to initialize,

     ••   The system has not been properly booted with a ZFS boot environment,

     ••   lliibbbbee fails to open the zpool the active boot environment resides on,
         or

     ••   lliibbbbee fails to locate the boot environment that is currently mounted.

     The lliibbbbee__cclloossee() function frees all resources previously acquired in
     lliibbbbee__iinniitt(), invalidating the handle in the process.

     The bbee__aaccttiivvee__nnaammee() function returns the name of the currently booted
     boot environment.  This boot environment may not belong to the same BE
     root as the root libbe is operating on!

     The bbee__aaccttiivvee__ppaatthh() function returns the full path of the currently
     booted boot environment.  This boot environment may not belong to the
     same BE root as the root libbe is operating on!

     The bbee__nneexxttbboooott__nnaammee() function returns the name of the boot environment
     that will be active on reboot.

     The bbee__nneexxttbboooott__ppaatthh() function returns the full path of the boot envi‐
     ronment that will be active on reboot.

     The bbee__rroooott__ppaatthh() function returns the boot environment root path.

     The bbee__ssnnaappsshhoott() function creates a snapshot of _b_e___n_a_m_e named _s_n_a_p___n_a_m_e.
     A value of NULL may be used, indicating that bbee__ssnnaapphhoott() should derive
     the snapshot name from the current date and time.  If _r_e_c_u_r_s_i_v_e is set,
     then bbee__ssnnaappsshhoott() will recursively snapshot the dataset.  If _r_e_s_u_l_t is
     not NULL, then it will be populated with the final “_b_e___n_a_m_e@_s_n_a_p___n_a_m_e”.

     The bbee__iiss__aauuttoo__ssnnaappsshhoott__nnaammee() function is used to determine if the given
     snapshot name matches the format that the bbee__ssnnaappsshhoott() function will use
     by default if it is not given a snapshot name to use.  It returns true if
     the name matches the format, and false if it does not.

     The bbee__ccrreeaattee() function creates a boot environment with the given name.
     The new boot environment will be created from a recursive snapshot of the
     currently booted boot environment.

     The bbee__ccrreeaattee__ddeepptthh() function creates a boot environment with the given
     name from an existing snapshot.  The depth parameter specifies the depth
     of recursion that will be cloned from the existing snapshot.  A depth of
     '0' is no recursion and '-1' is unlimited (i.e., a recursive boot envi‐
     ronment).

     The bbee__ccrreeaattee__ffrroomm__eexxiissttiinngg() function creates a boot environment with
     the given name from the name of an existing boot environment.  A recur‐
     sive snapshot will be made of the origin boot environment, and the new
     boot environment will be created from that.

     The bbee__ccrreeaattee__ffrroomm__eexxiissttiinngg__ssnnaapp() function creates a recursive boot en‐
     vironment with the given name from an existing snapshot.

